WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.896
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Grammar, level B two.

2
00:00:06.196 --> 00:00:09.768
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:10.068 --> 00:00:16.552
Unit twenty-eight: The Subjunctive. Today you will use base-form verbs after formal suggestions and demands.

4
00:00:16.852 --> 00:00:19.516
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:20.467 --> 00:00:23.688
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:24.550 --> 00:00:25.818
Suggest that.

7
00:00:26.817 --> 00:00:29.652
Suggest that means a verb that triggers the subjunctive.

8
00:00:30.250 --> 00:00:31.866
I suggest that he go.

9
00:00:32.450 --> 00:00:35.439
Your turn. Say: Suggest that.

10
00:00:38.300 --> 00:00:39.336
Suggest that.

11
00:00:40.083 --> 00:00:41.328
Insist that.

12
00:00:42.317 --> 00:00:44.688
Insist that means another triggering verb.

13
00:00:45.283 --> 00:00:47.422
She insisted that he apologise.

14
00:00:48.017 --> 00:00:50.553
Your turn. Say: Insist that.

15
00:00:53.400 --> 00:00:54.726
Insist that.

16
00:00:55.483 --> 00:00:56.635
It is vital that.

17
00:00:57.650 --> 00:01:00.544
It is vital that means an adjective phrase that triggers it.

18
00:01:01.150 --> 00:01:02.790
It is vital that she come.

19
00:01:03.383 --> 00:01:06.372
Your turn. Say: It is vital that.

20
00:01:09.233 --> 00:01:10.501
It is vital that.

21
00:01:11.250 --> 00:01:12.147
Were I.

22
00:01:13.150 --> 00:01:15.765
Were I means formal inversion for if I were.

23
00:01:16.350 --> 00:01:17.386
Were I rich...

24
00:01:17.983 --> 00:01:20.044
Your turn. Say: Were I.

25
00:01:22.900 --> 00:01:23.843
Were I.

26
00:01:24.583 --> 00:01:25.747
Base form.

27
00:01:26.750 --> 00:01:29.214
Base form means the verb without -s or -ed.

28
00:01:29.817 --> 00:01:31.062
Be, go, come.

29
00:01:31.650 --> 00:01:34.407
Your turn. Say: Base form.

30
00:01:37.267 --> 00:01:38.465
Base form.

31
00:01:39.217 --> 00:01:39.974
Formal.

32
00:01:40.983 --> 00:01:43.262
Formal means serious in style.

33
00:01:43.850 --> 00:01:45.223
A formal style.

34
00:01:45.817 --> 00:01:48.295
Your turn. Say: Formal.

35
00:01:51.133 --> 00:01:51.867
Formal.

36
00:01:52.617 --> 00:01:53.502
Demand.

37
00:01:54.517 --> 00:01:56.470
Demand means to ask strongly.

38
00:01:57.083 --> 00:01:58.700
They demand that he resign.

39
00:01:59.283 --> 00:02:01.506
Your turn. Say: Demand.

40
00:02:04.367 --> 00:02:05.391
Demand.

41
00:02:06.150 --> 00:02:07.174
Recommend.

42
00:02:08.183 --> 00:02:10.055
Recommend means to advise.

43
00:02:10.650 --> 00:02:12.383
I recommend that she rest.

44
00:02:12.983 --> 00:02:15.508
Your turn. Say: Recommend.

45
00:02:18.367 --> 00:02:19.333
Recommend.

46
00:02:20.133 --> 00:02:24.086
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:24.950 --> 00:02:28.749
Visal, complete: The manager insisted that every employee…

48
00:02:29.850 --> 00:02:42.777
The manager insisted that every employee wear a uniform. After verbs of suggestion and demand, the verb is in the base form, with no -s and no tense change.

49
00:02:43.883 --> 00:02:45.349
Which words trigger it?

50
00:02:46.450 --> 00:03:01.780
Suggest, recommend, insist, demand, propose, and adjectives like vital, essential, important: It is essential that he be present. The same form is used for every subject, even he and she.

51
00:03:02.883 --> 00:03:03.931
What about were?

52
00:03:05.017 --> 00:03:18.446
In formal if-clauses, were is used for all persons: If I were you. Were I to leave, I would tell you. British English often replaces the subjunctive with should: I suggest that he should go.

53
00:03:19.600 --> 00:03:21.205
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:22.050 --> 00:03:27.115
Grammar focus: Subjunctive: verb of demand plus that plus base verb.

55
00:03:27.415 --> 00:03:28.601
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:29.317 --> 00:03:31.200
I suggest that he be present.

57
00:03:32.117 --> 00:03:34.256
It is vital that she arrive on time.

58
00:03:35.150 --> 00:03:38.136
The manager insisted that everyone wear a uniform.

59
00:03:39.100 --> 00:03:48.837
After suggest, insist, demand, recommend, and vital / essential, use that + subject + base verb. No -s for he / she / it. Were for formal unreal if.

60
00:03:49.583 --> 00:03:53.188
Be careful! Don't say: I suggest that he is present.

61
00:03:55.133 --> 00:03:57.261
Say: I suggest that he be present.

62
00:03:57.561 --> 00:03:59.154
Use the base form.

63
00:03:59.967 --> 00:04:02.491
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:04:03.300 --> 00:04:04.684
Formal Demands.

65
00:04:04.984 --> 00:04:08.412
The manager insisted that every employee wear a uniform.

66
00:04:09.400 --> 00:04:11.806
I suggest that he be present at the meeting.

67
00:04:12.800 --> 00:04:14.858
It is vital that she arrive on time.

68
00:04:15.867 --> 00:04:18.447
The committee recommended that the plan be approved.

69
00:04:19.433 --> 00:04:22.164
British English often uses should in this structure.

70
00:04:23.267 --> 00:04:27.280
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:28.117 --> 00:04:30.058
I suggest that he blank present.

72
00:04:30.358 --> 00:04:33.187
A, be. B, is. C, was.

73
00:04:36.733 --> 00:04:38.361
The answer is A: be.

74
00:04:39.517 --> 00:04:41.632
It is essential that she blank early.

75
00:04:41.932 --> 00:04:45.226
A, arrives. B, arrived. C, arrive.

76
00:04:48.767 --> 00:04:50.929
The answer is C: arrive.

77
00:04:52.083 --> 00:04:53.688
They demanded that he blank.

78
00:04:53.988 --> 00:04:57.572
A, resign. B, resigns. C, resigned.

79
00:05:01.133 --> 00:05:02.982
The answer is A: resign.

80
00:05:04.117 --> 00:05:05.721
Which uses the subjunctive?

81
00:05:06.021 --> 00:05:12.136
A, He insisted that she goes.. B, He insisted she went.. C, He insisted that she go..

82
00:05:15.700 --> 00:05:18.698
The answer is C: He insisted that she go..

83
00:05:19.850 --> 00:05:23.370
According to the reading, what often replaces it in British English?

84
00:05:23.670 --> 00:05:26.650
A, should. B, would. C, might.

85
00:05:30.200 --> 00:05:32.281
The answer is A: should.

86
00:05:33.467 --> 00:05:36.502
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:05:37.350 --> 00:05:40.418
Complete: 'The manager insisted that every employee…'.

88
00:05:49.217 --> 00:05:50.659
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:05:50.959 --> 00:06:03.294
The manager insisted that every employee wear a uniform and be on time. I use the base form wear and be after insisted, with no -s and no tense change.

90
00:06:03.594 --> 00:06:05.257
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:06:06.150 --> 00:06:12.889
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and subjunctive: verb of demand plus that plus base verb.

92
00:06:13.189 --> 00:06:18.512
Today's value is precision of language. Choose your words carefully so others understand you.

93
00:06:18.812 --> 00:06:21.522
See you in Unit twenty-nine. Goodbye!

94
00:06:21.822 --> 00:06:24.358
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

